From: Xiaomi Mi MIX Linux port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wcd9335: add headset detection (MBHC); apq8096: headset jack

Mainline WCD9335 has the MBHC registers but no detection. Hook it to the
generic wcd-mbhc-v2 code, as WCD934x does: the MBHC register field table
and callbacks (from the downstream msm-3.18 WCD9335 driver), the MBHC and
HPH over-current interrupts in the regmap IRQ chip, and component
set_jack. Defaults follow WCD934x; the board's HPHL and ground switch
types come from DT (new binding properties).

The generic plug-type detection measures the mic line with the MBHC ADC,
which WCD9335 does not have (downstream used a separate legacy method):
on hardware every measurement timed out and the jack state flapped. A new
wcd_mbhc_config.mech_only makes the generic code report headphones from
the mechanical jack switch alone; WCD9335 sets it. No headset mic
detection yet. MICBIAS2 stays at its 1.8 V
reset value (0x10) in this driver. Button thresholds are unknown for any
WCD9335 board yet, so no buttons are configured. A failed MBHC init only
warns: playback and capture keep working.

apq8096 creates one "Headset Jack" (pins "Headphone Jack" and "Headset
Mic") for the first codec back end that supports set_jack; the init runs
for every back end, so the jack lives in per-card data and is set up once.

Mi MIX (lithium): stock sets msm-mbhc-hphl-swh = 1 and msm-mbhc-gnd-swh = 1
(stock DT lines 18835-18836), but with those as "normally closed" the jack
read inverted on hardware; the defaults read correctly, so the DT sets
neither. Headset mic on MICBIAS2 (18832-18833).

Based on a draft by the offline agent (artifacts/p11), reviewed and fixed.

---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-mbhc-v2.h
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-mbhc-v2.h
@@ -210,6 +210,8 @@
 	u32 moist_vref;
 	u32 moist_iref;
 	u32 moist_rref;
+	/* No plug-type ADC: report headphones from the mechanical switch alone */
+	bool mech_only;
 };
 
